WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.334 --> 00:00:03.734
-Republicans chose
Congressman Steve Scalise

00:00:03.734 --> 00:00:06.033
as their party's nominee
for Speaker of the House today,

00:00:06.033 --> 00:00:07.267
but it's still not clear

00:00:07.267 --> 00:00:09.100
if he actually has enough
votes to become speaker.

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:12.367
Many Republicans have criticized
the party's chaotic process,

00:00:12.367 --> 00:00:14.033
calling it absurd
and a mess.

00:00:14.033 --> 00:00:16.334
Also, one of those Republicans,
George Santos,

00:00:16.334 --> 00:00:19.334
just got charged again
with even more alleged crimes.

00:00:19.334 --> 00:00:21.334
For more on this,
it's time for A loser Look.

00:00:21.334 --> 00:00:23.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:25.267 --> 00:00:28.701
After deposing now former House
Speaker Kevin McCarthy last week

00:00:28.701 --> 00:00:30.434
and setting off
a chaotic chain of events,

00:00:30.434 --> 00:00:32.234
the House GOP
has finally selected

00:00:32.234 --> 00:00:35.000
a new nominee for speaker,
but that doesn't mean

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.267
he'll actually become
the next speaker of the House

00:00:37.267 --> 00:00:39.534
because, as we've learned
many times,

00:00:39.534 --> 00:00:42.067
Republicans can definitely
still screw things up.

00:00:42.067 --> 00:00:44.501
-There was a big vote
among Republicans

00:00:44.501 --> 00:00:46.701
in the House today
to determine a new speaker,

00:00:46.701 --> 00:00:50.167
and the GOP's nomination
for speaker

00:00:50.167 --> 00:00:52.400
has gone
to Steve Scalise,

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:54.868
the Republican congressman
from Louisiana,

00:00:54.868 --> 00:00:57.334
winning the GOP's nomination
for speaker

00:00:57.334 --> 00:00:58.968
on a secret ballot.

00:00:58.968 --> 00:01:00.701
-This is no guarantee
that Steve Scalise

00:01:00.701 --> 00:01:02.167
will be the next speaker
of the House.

00:01:02.167 --> 00:01:05.334
Republicans are still divided
as to how to take this process

00:01:05.334 --> 00:01:07.400
to the floor of the House
of Representatives.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:11.267
Already, there are members
of the Republican conference

00:01:11.267 --> 00:01:13.734
telling my colleague
Ali Vitali

00:01:13.734 --> 00:01:15.601
that they will not vote
for Steve Scalise

00:01:15.601 --> 00:01:17.133
on the floor of the House

00:01:17.133 --> 00:01:19.501
if and when
this speaker nomination

00:01:19.501 --> 00:01:21.133
actually makes it
to that stage.

00:01:21.133 --> 00:01:24.701
So the math is still a problem
for these Republican candidates.

00:01:24.701 --> 00:01:26.834
-Yes, math is still a problem
for Republicans.

00:01:26.834 --> 00:01:28.501
For example,
they're still not sure

00:01:28.501 --> 00:01:31.200
if 306 is more than 232.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:33.434
And, as we've seen before,

00:01:33.434 --> 00:01:36.434
winning -- winning
the GOP nomination for speaker

00:01:36.434 --> 00:01:38.968
definitely does not mean you
will actually become speaker.

00:01:38.968 --> 00:01:40.767
It's kind of like an actor
getting a callback

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:42.100
for a bit part on "Succession".

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:43.467
You didn't actually
get the part yet,

00:01:43.467 --> 00:01:44.534
and even if you do,

00:01:44.534 --> 00:01:45.734
you'll probably
just get yelled at,

00:01:45.734 --> 00:01:48.000
[Bleep] can by the end
of the episode.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.334
By the way, Scalise voted
to overturn the 2020 election,

00:01:51.334 --> 00:01:54.734
and in interviews, he's refused
to state without equivocation

00:01:54.734 --> 00:01:57.234
that Joe Biden won
and the election was not stolen.

00:01:57.234 --> 00:02:00.067
He's also refused to say that
Donald Trump was responsible

00:02:00.067 --> 00:02:02.934
for the coup attempt,
an insurrection, on January 6th.

00:02:02.934 --> 00:02:05.868
-When you met
with the former president,

00:02:05.868 --> 00:02:08.534
did you ask him
to take responsibility?

00:02:08.534 --> 00:02:11.033
Did he take responsibility?

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:14.100
-Well, Jonathan,
I was in Florida

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.300
doing some fundraising

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:16.834
throughout a number
of parts of Florida.

00:02:16.834 --> 00:02:18.501
I ended up at Mar a Lago,

00:02:18.501 --> 00:02:20.901
and the president reached out,
and we visited.

00:02:20.901 --> 00:02:22.734
-No one just ends up
at Mar a Lago.

00:02:22.734 --> 00:02:25.534
That's like telling your spouse
after a guy's trip,

00:02:25.534 --> 00:02:26.934
"We just went to a movie,
got dinner,

00:02:26.934 --> 00:02:28.267
and one thing led to another,
and we ended up

00:02:28.267 --> 00:02:30.934
at the Playboy Mansion.
It happens."

00:02:30.934 --> 00:02:33.834
Mar a Lago is a place you go to
for one of three reasons --

00:02:33.834 --> 00:02:36.367
kiss up to Trump,
a real bad wedding,

00:02:36.367 --> 00:02:38.734
or if you're a foreign spy,
looking at over here,

00:02:38.734 --> 00:02:41.501
our nation's nuclear secrets
at the dinner buffet.

00:02:41.501 --> 00:02:46.334
Side note -- what a plum gig
to be a spy sent to Mar a Lago.

00:02:46.334 --> 00:02:48.634
I mean, you don't have to know
how to break into a safe

00:02:48.634 --> 00:02:50.467
or avoid those
crisscross lasers.

00:02:50.467 --> 00:02:52.601
You never have to put on
a "Mission Impossible" mask.

00:02:52.601 --> 00:02:54.133
You just walk in the front door
and say,

00:02:54.133 --> 00:02:56.067
[Foreign accent] "Anyone here
know anything about submarines?"

00:02:56.067 --> 00:02:58.000
And the next thing you know,

00:02:58.000 --> 00:02:59.400
[Imitating Trump]
"I actually know quite a lot,

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:02.400
and I've got pictures of him
I'd love to show you.

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:04.367
I'd love to show them to you."

00:03:04.367 --> 00:03:06.667
[ Applause ]

00:03:06.667 --> 00:03:09.200
"Before, I just want to make
sure you are an American."

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:11.000
[Foreign accent]
"Yes, yes. From Cincinnati."

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:12.667
[ Laughter ]

00:03:12.667 --> 00:03:14.567
"Go Bengals."

00:03:16.767 --> 00:03:19.100
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:03:20.234 --> 00:03:21.634
[ Normal voice ]
And as if things couldn't get

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:23.434
any more chaotic
for Republicans,

00:03:23.434 --> 00:03:25.300
congressmen --
and according to him --

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:27.133
Taylor Swift's real boyfriend,

00:03:27.133 --> 00:03:29.834
George Santos,
just got charged again

00:03:29.834 --> 00:03:31.767
for allegedly
stealing campaign money

00:03:31.767 --> 00:03:34.167
and lying about basically
every part of his life.

00:03:34.167 --> 00:03:35.501
-Federal prosecutors hit

00:03:35.501 --> 00:03:37.801
embattled
Congressman George Santos

00:03:37.801 --> 00:03:40.801
with an array of stunning
new criminal charges,

00:03:40.801 --> 00:03:44.200
including wire fraud
and identity theft.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:45.634
The new accusations
were made

00:03:45.634 --> 00:03:48.501
in a 23 count
superseding indictment.

00:03:48.501 --> 00:03:50.767
-Republican Congressman
George Santos

00:03:50.767 --> 00:03:53.601
now faces more criminal charges.

00:03:53.601 --> 00:03:55.167
And these include wire fraud,

00:03:55.167 --> 00:03:57.100
falsifying records,
and identity theft.

00:03:57.100 --> 00:03:58.667
That's among other crimes.

00:03:58.667 --> 00:04:00.968
Prosecutors now accusing Santos
of being involved

00:04:00.968 --> 00:04:03.701
in a credit card scheme
where the campaign

00:04:03.701 --> 00:04:06.667
would charge contributors
credit cards repeatedly

00:04:06.667 --> 00:04:09.634
and above
the federal contribution limits.

00:04:09.634 --> 00:04:11.701
-He illegally charged
their credit cards.

00:04:11.701 --> 00:04:13.000
He's less like a member
of Congress

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:14.601
and more like
a telemarketer scam

00:04:14.601 --> 00:04:16.367
your grandpa would fall for.

00:04:16.367 --> 00:04:17.667
[Imitating old man]
"The man said if I gave him

00:04:17.667 --> 00:04:20.934
my credit card, he'd send me
gold bars in the mail.

00:04:20.934 --> 00:04:25.133
I believed him because
he's a star volleyball player.

00:04:25.133 --> 00:04:28.200
Who would lie
about such a thing?"

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:29.701
[ Normal voice ]
Is there a crime George Santos

00:04:29.701 --> 00:04:31.200
hasn't been accused of?

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:32.801
I'm just waiting for the day
you watch the news

00:04:32.801 --> 00:04:35.100
and prosecutors say Santos
illegally charged

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:36.968
donors credit cards,
stole their identities,

00:04:36.968 --> 00:04:38.767
and refused to pick up
his dog's poop.

00:04:38.767 --> 00:04:41.267
And also, it wasn't his dog,
it was a cat dressed as a dog,

00:04:41.267 --> 00:04:43.334
which he used to pretend
he was blind

00:04:43.334 --> 00:04:45.000
to get preferential
seating on an airplane,

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:46.534
which he paid
for using fake bills

00:04:46.534 --> 00:04:48.167
that he printed
at a Kinko's, a Kinko's,

00:04:48.167 --> 00:04:50.400
which he broke into at night
using a golf club

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:51.968
he claimed was a gift
from Tiger Woods,

00:04:51.968 --> 00:04:54.033
but which, in fact,
he stole from a child

00:04:54.033 --> 00:04:56.167
at a putt putt course.

00:04:56.167 --> 00:04:58.100
And it won't surprise you
to learn that Santos

00:04:58.100 --> 00:05:01.100
did not want to discuss
these latest charges.

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:03.100
Here he is once again
being chased down

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:05.634
the halls of Congress
by a group of reporters

00:05:05.634 --> 00:05:07.300
claiming he didn't even know
about the charges

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:09.167
because he didn't have access
to his phone.

00:05:09.167 --> 00:05:11.334
-No comment. I was -- I did not
have access to my phone.

00:05:11.334 --> 00:05:12.734
I have no clue.
-Prosecutors say you defrauded

00:05:12.734 --> 00:05:14.234
the American public.
Will you resign?

00:05:14.234 --> 00:05:15.467
-I have no clue of what you guys
are talking about.

00:05:15.467 --> 00:05:17.934
No, I will not. Excuse me.
-They said that you

00:05:17.934 --> 00:05:19.033
stole people's identities.

00:05:19.033 --> 00:05:22.067
Did you steal
people's identities?

00:05:22.067 --> 00:05:23.634
Did you commit identity fraud?
-Are you still gonna vote

00:05:23.634 --> 00:05:26.100
at the speakers election?
-What do you have to say

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:27.434
to your constituents?
-Will you step down?

00:05:27.434 --> 00:05:29.334
-I will not.
I have no comment.

00:05:29.334 --> 00:05:31.567
I was in conference like
everyone else, without my phone,

00:05:31.567 --> 00:05:33.200
so I have nothing to talk about.

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:35.567
I need to take a look at --
-Did you commit wire fraud?

00:05:35.567 --> 00:05:37.834
That was a pretty
basic question.

00:05:37.834 --> 00:05:38.901
-First of all,
when this is over,

00:05:38.901 --> 00:05:40.334
Santos is either going
to be in jail

00:05:40.334 --> 00:05:42.434
or running the last leg
of the U.S. relay team.

00:05:42.434 --> 00:05:44.934
I mean, no member of Congress
has ever gotten

00:05:44.934 --> 00:05:46.334
so much cardio out of the job.

00:05:46.334 --> 00:05:49.801
Second, there's no way
that's a real phone call.

00:05:49.801 --> 00:05:51.734
The screen does look
like a phone call,

00:05:51.734 --> 00:05:53.200
but when you zoom into it,
it says

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:54.801
"Fake call
to ignore reporters."

00:05:54.801 --> 00:05:56.567
[ Laughter ]

00:05:56.567 --> 00:05:58.601
Nothing sums up George Santos
more than claiming

00:05:58.601 --> 00:06:00.701
he didn't have access
to his phone

00:06:00.701 --> 00:06:03.000
while talking on his phone.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:04.167
Unless that's not his phone

00:06:04.167 --> 00:06:05.801
and he stole it
from someone's grandpa.

00:06:05.801 --> 00:06:07.300
[ Imitating old man ]
"Joke's on you.

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:10.834
I'll just buy a new one
when I get my gold bars.

00:06:10.834 --> 00:06:12.701
Thank you, volleyball man."

00:06:12.701 --> 00:06:14.834
[ Normal voice ] Also,
not having access to your phone

00:06:14.834 --> 00:06:16.133
is such a lame excuse.

00:06:16.133 --> 00:06:18.801
It's a 23 count indictment,
not a text from your mom.

00:06:18.801 --> 00:06:21.834
Maybe one of your aides could,
I don't know, come up,

00:06:21.834 --> 00:06:23.000
give you a heads up.

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:24.701
I've been interrupted
during meetings

00:06:24.701 --> 00:06:26.367
for way less important things.

00:06:26.367 --> 00:06:27.667
One time, I was in the middle
of a meeting

00:06:27.667 --> 00:06:29.901
about our show's budget,
and someone from wardrobe

00:06:29.901 --> 00:06:33.701
came in to ask me if I wanted
to try on the cicada headpiece.

00:06:33.701 --> 00:06:36.300
And then I turn on C-Span
and [Bleep] George Santos

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:39.200
is wearing it.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:42.334
So one of the GOP's members
has been indicted again,

00:06:42.334 --> 00:06:45.000
as Republicans embark on yet
another chaotic fight

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:46.000
over the next speaker.

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:47.434
It hasn't even been a year

00:06:47.434 --> 00:06:49.934
since Republicans won a very
small majority in the House,

00:06:49.934 --> 00:06:51.968
and in that time,
they've seen indictments

00:06:51.968 --> 00:06:54.133
and humiliating scandals
and nearly broken out

00:06:54.133 --> 00:06:55.801
into physical fighting
multiple times.

00:06:55.801 --> 00:06:57.901
You might recall
that in January,

00:06:57.901 --> 00:06:59.601
one Republican member
of Congress

00:06:59.601 --> 00:07:01.367
had to be restrained
by his face

00:07:01.367 --> 00:07:03.000
from lunging at
a Republican colleague

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:04.334
during a late night
vote for speaker.

00:07:04.334 --> 00:07:07.000
And then, a fellow
Republican explained

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:09.367
that moment in a way that made
it even more embarrassing.

00:07:09.367 --> 00:07:11.667
Again, this is a Republican
member of Congress

00:07:11.667 --> 00:07:13.868
talking about his fellow
Republican congressman.

00:07:13.868 --> 00:07:15.300
Quote...

00:07:19.734 --> 00:07:22.100
Interesting fact, rednecks are
the only members of Congress

00:07:22.100 --> 00:07:23.701
legally allowed to drink
on the House floor.

00:07:23.701 --> 00:07:24.868
This is true.

00:07:24.868 --> 00:07:26.701
If you bring a bourbon
on the House floor,

00:07:26.701 --> 00:07:28.567
you'll be ordered to leave,
unless you know

00:07:28.567 --> 00:07:30.400
the first names
of both Duke boys

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:32.334
and the car they drove.

00:07:32.334 --> 00:07:33.968
[ Southern accent ] "The member
from Kentucky is out of order

00:07:33.968 --> 00:07:35.501
unless he can name
the main characters

00:07:35.501 --> 00:07:36.601
from the 'Dukes of Hazzard'."

00:07:36.601 --> 00:07:38.968
"Bo and Luke
and the General Lee. Whoo.

00:07:38.968 --> 00:07:41.801
Them boys was crazy."

00:07:41.801 --> 00:07:43.534
[ Normal voice ]
You may proceed.

00:07:43.534 --> 00:07:45.400
Seriously, calling Republicans
drunk rednecks

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:47.934
is the kind of thing even I
couldn't say about Republicans.

00:07:47.934 --> 00:07:50.868
Like, if we put that in
an early draft of A Closer Look

00:07:50.868 --> 00:07:51.968
and then read through it,

00:07:51.968 --> 00:07:53.400
I'd get a note
from one of our producers

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:55.934
saying that joke might be
insensitive to alcoholics,

00:07:55.934 --> 00:07:57.267
Republicans, and rednecks.

00:07:57.267 --> 00:07:59.667
And look, I'm not going to say
who that producer is,

00:07:59.667 --> 00:08:03.167
but her name rhymes
with blemily blerotas,

00:08:03.167 --> 00:08:05.300
who's very sensitive
because she's from Indianapolis,

00:08:05.300 --> 00:08:06.634
which doesn't mean
she's a redneck.

00:08:06.634 --> 00:08:08.934
It just means they're definitely
within driving distance.

00:08:08.934 --> 00:08:10.167
So...

00:08:10.167 --> 00:08:12.734
[ Laughter ]

00:08:12.734 --> 00:08:14.200
That was back in January.

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:16.667
Then last week, Republicans
erupted in chaos again

00:08:16.667 --> 00:08:19.067
and deposed their short
lived speaker, Kevin McCarthy.

00:08:19.067 --> 00:08:21.467
And again, they nearly
came to blows.

00:08:21.467 --> 00:08:22.934
-Jake, I'll be really candid.

00:08:22.934 --> 00:08:25.567
I think if we had
stayed together

00:08:25.567 --> 00:08:26.801
in the meeting last night,

00:08:26.801 --> 00:08:28.634
I think that you would
have seen fists thrown.

00:08:28.634 --> 00:08:30.601
And I'm not being dramatic
when I say that.

00:08:30.601 --> 00:08:33.734
There is a lot of raw emotions
right now.

00:08:33.734 --> 00:08:35.734
-Booze, fighting,
and raw emotions.

00:08:35.734 --> 00:08:37.801
Is this Congress
or an Irish wake?

00:08:37.801 --> 00:08:38.968
You think you miss Sheamus?

00:08:38.968 --> 00:08:40.934
"I miss Sheamus
more than you, boy-o.

00:08:40.934 --> 00:08:41.968
Now, let's take it outside.

00:08:41.968 --> 00:08:43.400
And remember,
no grabbing of the face.

00:08:43.400 --> 00:08:46.400
This isn't Congress."

00:08:46.400 --> 00:08:47.868
I can't imagine
another workplace

00:08:47.868 --> 00:08:50.901
where you're allowed to say
good thing we ended that meeting

00:08:50.901 --> 00:08:53.868
because we're about to beat
the [Bleep] out of each other.

00:08:53.868 --> 00:08:57.200
Like, again, I know I would
immediately get a call from HR

00:08:57.200 --> 00:08:58.434
if I said something like that

00:08:58.434 --> 00:08:59.968
after a pitch meeting
with my writers.

00:08:59.968 --> 00:09:03.133
Although, if my writers land
a punch like they land a joke,

00:09:03.133 --> 00:09:04.968
then I got nothing
to worry about.

00:09:04.968 --> 00:09:07.968
[ Laughter ]

00:09:09.601 --> 00:09:12.601
Oh, don't take this out.
I'll take 'em all on.

00:09:14.267 --> 00:09:17.167
The depths of the GOP's
insanity were on full display

00:09:17.167 --> 00:09:19.767
yesterday when South Carolina
Congresswoman Nancy Mace

00:09:19.767 --> 00:09:21.901
showed up to the House
GOP meetings wearing a shirt

00:09:21.901 --> 00:09:23.501
with a giant letter
A on it.

00:09:23.501 --> 00:09:25.634
Mace voted to oust
McCarthy last week,

00:09:25.634 --> 00:09:27.400
and she said
she was wearing the shirt

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:29.634
as a response to all
the attacks against her.

00:09:29.634 --> 00:09:32.868
-Congresswoman Nancy Mace,
she had a new letter.

00:09:32.868 --> 00:09:35.467
Wearing a T-shirt
with a big red letter "A".

00:09:35.467 --> 00:09:38.934
She was one of the Republicans
who ousted Kevin McCarthy.

00:09:38.934 --> 00:09:40.534
-I'm wearing the Scarlet letter

00:09:40.534 --> 00:09:42.834
after the week
that I just had last week,

00:09:42.834 --> 00:09:45.868
being a woman up here
and being demonized for my vote

00:09:45.868 --> 00:09:47.267
and for my voice.

00:09:47.267 --> 00:09:49.968
-Did Republicans also ban
the book "The Scarlet Letter"?

00:09:49.968 --> 00:09:51.934
Because clearly
you haven't read it.

00:09:51.934 --> 00:09:53.400
The A stands for "adulterer",

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:55.968
not, as I presume
you're using it, "A-hole".

00:09:55.968 --> 00:09:58.501
Also, if memory serves,

00:09:58.501 --> 00:10:01.000
the A was a mark of humiliation,
not a fashion statement.

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:02.901
Hester Prynne wasn't
walking around Boston

00:10:02.901 --> 00:10:04.567
with a scarlet letter
pinned to her chest going,

00:10:04.567 --> 00:10:06.834
[ English accent ]
"Oh, check me out.

00:10:06.834 --> 00:10:09.133
I just had an illicit affair
during Puritan times.

00:10:09.133 --> 00:10:11.033
Jealous much?"

00:10:11.033 --> 00:10:12.501
[ Normal voice ] And look,
I know people didn't

00:10:12.501 --> 00:10:14.434
have that accent in the 1600's,

00:10:14.434 --> 00:10:16.701
but isn't it fun
to think they did?

00:10:16.701 --> 00:10:18.701
All great literature
that took place in New England

00:10:18.701 --> 00:10:19.868
can be enhanced
if you imagine

00:10:19.868 --> 00:10:21.033
the people were talking
like that.

00:10:21.033 --> 00:10:22.167
"The Crucible" --
[English accent] "This town

00:10:22.167 --> 00:10:25.033
is [Bleep] crawling
with witches, kid."

00:10:25.033 --> 00:10:26.033
[ Normal voice ]
"Little women" --

00:10:26.033 --> 00:10:27.033
[English accent]
What's up with Beth?

00:10:27.033 --> 00:10:29.601
She looks pekid.

00:10:29.601 --> 00:10:30.767
[ Normal voice ]
"Ethan Frome" --

00:10:30.767 --> 00:10:32.033
[English accent] Look who
the cat dragged in.

00:10:32.033 --> 00:10:33.467
Ethan [Bleep] Frome.

00:10:33.467 --> 00:10:35.767
[ Normal voice ] I've never
read that book, so I don't...

00:10:35.767 --> 00:10:38.000
[ Laughter ]

00:10:40.834 --> 00:10:43.167
[ English accent ] "Yo, Ethan."

00:10:43.167 --> 00:10:44.467
[ Normal voice ]
Seriously, though, Nancy Bass,

00:10:44.467 --> 00:10:45.834
you look like you just walked
out of a school play

00:10:45.834 --> 00:10:47.200
or a football game.

00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:49.200
Somewhere, there's a group
of Packers fans missing an A

00:10:49.200 --> 00:10:51.567
who are very upset.

00:10:51.567 --> 00:10:53.133
And even anchors
are having a hard time

00:10:53.133 --> 00:10:54.400
taking Republicans seriously.

00:10:54.400 --> 00:10:58.133
Here's CNN's Jake Tapper
reacting to Mace's PR stunt.

00:10:58.133 --> 00:11:01.300
-Congresswoman Nancy Mace
walked in with a letter A

00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:03.501
on her shirt as she walked
into closed doors.

00:11:03.501 --> 00:11:05.267
She was asked by her colleague,
Annie Grayer,

00:11:05.267 --> 00:11:06.300
what that was about.

00:11:06.300 --> 00:11:08.767
She said it was
a Scarlet Letter.

00:11:08.767 --> 00:11:10.000
Jake.

00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:12.000
-Okay.

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:13.634
That's not making me convinced

00:11:13.634 --> 00:11:15.667
that they have
their act together.

00:11:15.667 --> 00:11:18.567
Damn, you just got sassed
by Jake Tapper,

00:11:18.567 --> 00:11:22.267
AKA, you just got tapped.
-Tapped.

00:11:22.267 --> 00:11:25.267
[ Horns blow ]
[ Electrical guitar plays ]

00:11:28.968 --> 00:11:31.634
[ Laughter ]

00:11:33.701 --> 00:11:36.067
-I do wish news anchors
were more sarcastic.

00:11:36.067 --> 00:11:37.701
It's fun to imagine
Walter Cronkite

00:11:37.701 --> 00:11:40.701
using that same tone
to report on Apollo 11.

00:11:40.701 --> 00:11:43.567
[ Sarcastic tone ] "American
astronauts successfully

00:11:43.567 --> 00:11:44.968
landed on the moon,

00:11:44.968 --> 00:11:49.334
which scientists say is almost
as charmless and dusty

00:11:49.334 --> 00:11:50.968
as yo mama."

00:11:50.968 --> 00:11:53.968
[ Laughter ]

00:11:56.834 --> 00:11:58.100
[ Normal voice ]
And the dysfunction

00:11:58.100 --> 00:12:00.167
isn't just paralyzing
the GOP conference,

00:12:00.167 --> 00:12:02.534
it's threatening to paralyze
the entire U.S. government.

00:12:02.534 --> 00:12:05.367
Again, here is a Republican
member of Congress

00:12:05.367 --> 00:12:08.334
explaining the stakes
of this GOP leadership dispute.

00:12:08.334 --> 00:12:11.334
-Funding the government
is part of our fundamental duty,

00:12:11.334 --> 00:12:12.901
and we can't even do that.

00:12:12.901 --> 00:12:15.834
So... And now, here we are
at the 11th hour

00:12:15.834 --> 00:12:19.868
with a clock ticking,
and we can't even see a speaker.

00:12:19.868 --> 00:12:21.434
Man, that says volumes.

00:12:21.434 --> 00:12:23.701
At first,
it was somewhat comical.

00:12:23.701 --> 00:12:28.167
Now, it's on -- it's bordering
on the -- on the absurd.

00:12:28.167 --> 00:12:29.334
-Bordering on the absurd.

00:12:29.334 --> 00:12:30.701
One of your members
is walking around

00:12:30.701 --> 00:12:32.234
like a [Bleep]
"Sesame Street" character

00:12:32.234 --> 00:12:35.300
who hangs out near Oscar's
trash cans selling drugs.

00:12:35.300 --> 00:12:37.100
"Hey, hey, hey, Elmo.
You want to get high?

00:12:37.100 --> 00:12:38.567
The A stands
for amphetamines."

00:12:38.567 --> 00:12:42.767
Now, even Republicans
are admitting in public

00:12:42.767 --> 00:12:44.334
they're incapable
of governing.

00:12:44.334 --> 00:12:45.834
Again, that's not me
saying that.

00:12:45.834 --> 00:12:47.868
I'm sure there's some viewers
who accidentally tune

00:12:47.868 --> 00:12:50.234
into this show and think,
"Oh, there's Myers ranting again

00:12:50.234 --> 00:12:51.767
about how Republicans
suck at their jobs."

00:12:51.767 --> 00:12:53.300
But this time,
it's not me saying it.

00:12:53.300 --> 00:12:54.467
It's a Republican saying it.

00:12:54.467 --> 00:12:56.133
In fact, I'm going to repeat
those exact words

00:12:56.133 --> 00:12:58.234
you just heard from that
Republican congressman,

00:12:58.234 --> 00:13:00.133
but I'm going to do it like
it's the intro to A Closer Look

00:13:00.133 --> 00:13:01.334
in a segment we're calling

00:13:01.334 --> 00:13:02.567
See If You Can Tell
the Difference Between

00:13:02.567 --> 00:13:04.133
Seth Talking About
Republicans and Republicans

00:13:04.133 --> 00:13:06.367
Talking about Republicans.

00:13:06.367 --> 00:13:07.701
Alright. Here we go.

00:13:07.701 --> 00:13:09.601
Funding the government is part
of the Republican Party's

00:13:09.601 --> 00:13:11.334
fundamental duty,
and they can't even do that.

00:13:11.334 --> 00:13:13.667
So now, here we are at the 11th
hour with the clock ticking,

00:13:13.667 --> 00:13:15.734
and they can't even see
the speaker, which says volumes.

00:13:15.734 --> 00:13:17.234
At first, it was
somewhat comical.

00:13:17.234 --> 00:13:18.567
Now, it's bordering
on the absurd.

00:13:18.567 --> 00:13:20.801
For more on this,
it's time for A Closer Look.

00:13:24.100 --> 00:13:26.634
Nancy Mace, what grade
do we get for that bit?

00:13:26.634 --> 00:13:27.868
Yes!

00:13:27.868 --> 00:13:29.100
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:13:29.100 --> 00:13:30.367
So...

00:13:30.367 --> 00:13:31.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:13:31.467 --> 00:13:33.167
Republicans have,
by their own admission,

00:13:33.167 --> 00:13:34.701
paralyzed one chamber
of Congress

00:13:34.701 --> 00:13:36.634
because of their ineptitude
and dysfunction.

00:13:36.634 --> 00:13:38.067
They're admitting to the world
they're not

00:13:38.067 --> 00:13:40.601
a serious governing party,
and still, no one can predict

00:13:40.601 --> 00:13:42.100
when this pointless
melodrama will end.

00:13:42.100 --> 00:13:44.167
On the bright side,
maybe they'll finally

00:13:44.167 --> 00:13:46.133
have enough downtime to read

00:13:46.133 --> 00:13:48.334
that book they love about
a woman named...

00:13:48.334 --> 00:13:49.868
-"Scarlet Letter".

00:13:49.868 --> 00:13:51.334
-[ Chuckles ]
[ Laughter ]

00:13:51.334 --> 00:13:53.133
This has been A Closer Look.

